  "description": "North Carolina's 7th Congressional District covers southeastern North Carolina including parts of Fayetteville and Wilmington. Incumbent Republican David Rouzer, first elected in 2014, is seeking re-election. He faces Democrat Kimberly Hardy, an associate professor at Fayetteville State University, along with Libertarian Maad Abu-Ghazalah and independent Michael Henry. The district has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+7, making it a safely Republican seat in a midterm cycle that will determine control of the U.S. House.",
